#note "[STALE MECHANISM, corrected 2026-08-27] NonEmptyGuardInliner was DELETED (Fix #367 / EC-100) and no guard is injected at load any more; the expectation below still holds, but for the rule's AUTHORED Requirements/Check, not for the injection this note describes. Pins the MACHINE-DERIVED guard: the shipped Check reads '... and var_exists(TRTEMFL) and TRTEMFL != Y' because NonEmptyGuardInliner arm 5 wraps a negative comparison against a string literal, and that conjunct folds FALSE on an absent column, so the rule EXECUTES and stays silent. That guard is DERIVED - it must never be written into the rule. PLAN-retire-corpus-transforms phase 4: the rule now declares the gate variable in Requirements.Variables.All, so the absent column takes the auditable SKIP this scenario pins (Fix #330 remedy: a presence rule reports the absence once)."
